# Architecture boundaries

Read `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE_BASELINE_INDEX.md` and `docs/decisions/ADR_INDEX.md`.

- Project B architecture is frozen for the bounded sprint.
- Project B owns tenant/coach/client/journey runtime; Database/Canonical owns canonical knowledge, provenance and KDB semantics.
- Preserve fail-closed effective access, tenant isolation, immutable published journey versions, governed canonical promotion and reconstructable audit/outbox.
- Do not move Canonical truth into Project B or Project B behavior into KDB.
- Do not introduce a new framework, service, repository or deployment boundary without an accepted ADR.
- Stop and create an owner-return when implementation requires architecture reopening.